## WHAT TO BUILD (property first; the plants are the proof)
**General property (binding):** *the branch's final diff against `origin/main` is exactly the four paths of round 1, all additions (`git diff --name-status` prints four `A` lines); the diff from `a5f3add1` to your head touches only `tests/e2e/shell-layout.spec.js` (and the config only under item 2); the two data files keep their blobs; the record a run of the fixed spec writes is byte-equal to the committed record; no `.skip`, `.only`, `test.fixme`, `waitForTimeout`, `setTimeout`, sleep, `eval`, `new Function`, suppression comment, `existsSync`/`statSync`/`accessSync`/`lstatSync`, child-process call or shell string is added; no person's name, decision-card id, B-number, plant id or ticket key appears in any added line (the commit SUBJECT may name RD-928); added lines ASCII, no TAB, no CR.* **Any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP.**

### Item 1 (Major): decide the write by the final component, in the call that creates the file
**Property:** *the record file is created by ONE open call with create-exclusive semantics (`fs.openSync(target, 'wx', 0o600)` is the shape) on `target` = the real path of the directory part (already shown to lie inside the temp roots) joined with the final name; a final component that is a link (to an existing or to a missing file) or any existing file or directory is refused with a message that begins `REFUSING TO WRITE` and names the temp directory, BEFORE any byte is written; the bytes go through the descriptor that open returned and the descriptor is closed in a `finally`; the sha256 logged at `:609` is computed from the bytes written, not read back by path; no stat, exists, access or lstat call is added.* The existing refusals stay as they are: a plain path outside the roots, a dot-dot escape, a link in the DIRECTORY part.
**Why this shape (the choice the residue asked for):** the residue offers three fixes. (a) `lstat` then write decides and acts in two calls, so a link swapped in between is followed: a check-to-use race, the shape `js/file-system-race` names. (b) `O_NOFOLLOW` with truncate refuses a link but still opens and truncates any pre-existing file at the name, including a hard link that points at a file elsewhere (DERIVED, not run). (c) `mkdtempSync` plus a fixed name changes the path the operator names and the gate's `cmp` flow. `'wx'` is `O_CREAT|O_EXCL`: the kernel makes the decision and the creation in one step, and POSIX makes `O_EXCL` fail on a link whatever it points to. Using the REAL directory path for the open (not the operator's string) also removes the gap between the directory check and the open for the directory part (DERIVED: the real path has no link in it at the check; a later swap of a real directory for a link needs write rights on its parent). **The cost, stated:** a run that names an existing file now fails after the work (about 3 to 6 minutes), so every record run names a path that does not exist yet; the header says so (below). The gate and the builder's own earlier hand-over used a fixed `/tmp/x.json`: tell Tuesday in FOR TUESDAY.
**Shape of the code (a route; the property binds):** replace `assertTempPath` by `tempRoots()` and `writeRecordFile(p, text, roots = tempRoots())` that does the directory check against `roots`, builds `target`, opens with `'wx'`, writes through the descriptor, returns the sha256 of the bytes; the PRODUCT test calls it in place of `:607`-`:609`. Keep the logged line `[shell-layout] record written to <out> (sha256 <hex>)` as it is.
**The control (the regression probe of the residue, as a fourth CONTROL test, `tests/e2e/shell-layout.spec.js`):** `CONTROL: a record path that is a link or already exists is refused, and nothing outside the temp directory is written`. It builds a sandbox with `fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'nexusai-shell-layout-ctl-'))` (push it onto `state.made`, which `afterAll` removes, `:576`-`:582`), with `allowed/` and `outside/` inside it, calls the SAME `writeRecordFile` with `roots` = the real path of `allowed/` (the test seam: the production call uses the default roots), and requires: (1) a link `allowed/link.json` to `outside/target.json` (holding a known string) is refused with `REFUSING TO WRITE` and `temp directory` in the message, and the outside file reads back byte-equal to the known string; (2) a dangling link to `outside/absent.json` is refused and `outside/` still lists exactly `target.json` (use `readdirSync`, not an exists call); (3) an existing regular file in `allowed/` is refused and keeps its content; (4) a plain path in `outside/` is refused and not created; (5) a new name in `allowed/` is written, content equal to the text given, and the returned sha256 equals the one computed from that text. Every expected value hand-written. **Red-first (PC0): write the function FIRST in its OLD logic (directory check, then `writeFileSync` by path) with the `roots` seam, add the control, run it alone (`--grep 'CONTROL: a record path'`): it must be RED on cases (1) and (3) with the first reason line printed (an `undefined` or a typo is not a red), (2) red or green as the old logic does (print it), (4) and (5) green. Then change the function to the property; the control is green.** The runtime plant P1 below is the same defect through the whole spec.
**Header words (`:64`, `:72`-`:75`, `:77`):** say the record path must not exist yet, that a link or an existing file is refused, and that there are four controls (the new one is not a mutation control: say so in one sentence). No other header change.

